<section style="padding:0 0 130px"><div class="wrap">
  <p class="label red" style="margin:0 0 20px">How we fix it</p>
  <h2 class="disp" style="font-size:clamp(36px,4.5vw,58px);margin:0 0 56px;max-width:820px">Three steps, in this order.</h2>
  <div class="g3"><div class="card reveal" style="min-height:240px"><p class="label" style="margin:0 0 14px">Step 01</p><h3 class="disp" style="font-size:28px;margin:0 0 12px">Collect the real questions</h3><p class="p" style="font-size:15px">Search data, reviews, support tickets and sales conversations. The words buyers use are rarely the words in your catalog.</p></div><div class="card reveal" style="min-height:240px"><p class="label" style="margin:0 0 14px">Step 02</p><h3 class="disp" style="font-size:28px;margin:0 0 12px">Map each question to one page</h3><p class="p" style="font-size:15px">Every article has one job and one next step, usually a collection or product the reader can click through to.</p></div><div class="card reveal" style="min-height:240px"><p class="label" style="margin:0 0 14px">Step 03</p><h3 class="disp" style="font-size:28px;margin:0 0 12px">Write, check, publish on a schedule</h3><p class="p" style="font-size:15px">Articles are written to answer the question better than the current top result, then published on a calendar you approve.</p></div></div>
</div></section>
